{
  "name": "crocodile",
  "_about": "SCULPTED (2026-11-05, docs/engines.md 'the sculpt overlay'): a Nile crocodile 3.6 m long -- a low, wide trunk with a pale belly, sprawled limbs (upper bones out sideways, forearms and shanks down, the hind longer), six rows of keeled osteoderms in transverse bands down the back, a deep, laterally flattened tail with two crests of upright scutes joining into one, dark tail bands with pale interbands; a flat skull table with raised orbits, a long flat snout with the nostril bulb, the teeth showing along the shut jaws SHARP PASS 2 (2026-11-08): the pointed parts -- toothL, toothU (11 in all) -- are the engine's sharp `horn`s (sharp.js), made from the field shapes they replaced by tools/creaturegen/sharp/ (claws.py, teeth.py, spikes.py, antlers.py, bills.py): rooted in the body, tips pointed; RE-RUN those after this species' generator. (2026-11-08, review.py: teeth) The TEETH stand on the jaw margin (the slit where the jaws shut): each upper a cone out of the upper jaw by the slit, standing a little out from the lower jaw's outer face; the lowers between them, up over the upper jaw; the enlarged 4th lower in the notch behind the rosette; round, curved slightly back, the root faired into a gum (horn `fair`), stained toward it. (2026-11-08, review.py: jaw line) The JAW LINE shows where the teeth stand: the groove (`lipCut`) and the dark lip along the slit moved out onto the face (they lay inside the snout, written for a narrower jaw, so no line showed and the teeth seemed to stand up the side of the face).",
